<title>BOTSWANA: Botswana's Inco up 18% after-tax.</title>
<headline>Botswana's Inco up 18% after-tax.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended Oct 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (thebe)		 75    vs    55</p>
<p>    Final div (thebe)	 4.5   vs    6.2</p>
<p>     making total (thebe)   7.5   vs    6.2</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     1.43  vs    1.22</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     1.76  vs    1.39</p>
<p>    Tax			   0.33  vs    0.17</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     0.05  vs    0.15</p>
<p>    Turnover		   14.27  vs   12.39</p>
<p>Div payable March 14 1997</p>
<p>On register February 28 1997</p>
<p>Full name: Inco Holdings Limited</p>
<p>NOTE - The directors said in a statement that the company continued to show good growth and consolidate its market share. The balance sheet (net asset value up 22 per cent to 57.1 thebe per share) and cash reserves (up 125 per cent to 1.51 million pula) had been strengthened for possible developments during 1997.</p>
<p>-- Gaborone newsroom +267 347182</p>
